{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00488 - MONDO_3792",
  "verbalization": "Altretamine, a chemotherapy agent, is linked to Ovarian Carcinosarcoma through a series of indications involving Rucaparib, a poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase (PARP) inhibitor. The evidence suggests that Altretamine may be repurposed for the treatment of ovarian carcinosarcoma, as it is associated with both Ovarian Adenocarcinoma and Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, which in turn are linked to Rucaparib. This indicates a potential pathway where Altretamine could exert therapeutic effects through a shared mechanism with Rucaparib, possibly targeting cancer cells through PARP inhibition or other molecular pathways. The high scores in the evidence suggest a strong, biologically plausible link, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Rucaparib and Ovarian Carcinosarcoma supports the hypothesis that Altretamine may have a role in the treatment of this malignancy, though further studies are needed to confirm the specific mechanism and clinical relevance.",
